  "history": {
    "origins": "Traditional Navajo card game played among Navajo communities in the USA. The Navajo name is Neeznáá Dah Yíjihí or sometimes Da'aka' (general word for card game). A documented variant uses a double deck with 80 cards and meld-11 Conquian-style play for 2–7 players; fishing-style capture versions summing to ten are also played in Navajo communities.",
    "originCountries": [
      "USA"
    ],
    "timeline": [
      "20th century: Traditional Navajo fishing game played in Navajo communities in the USA."
    ],
    "evolution": "Variant of fishing games with capture mechanics adapted for Navajo play traditions.",
